Goal:- There is a unprotected admin functionality. We have to find admin pannel and delete a user.

Observation:- The link to the admin pannel was disclosed in robots.txt 
                as  /administrator-panel

Steps to solve :- 

        Step1:- Access the lab
        Step2:- Search for robots.txt by changing the Url
        Step3:- there is a disclosre to admin pannel 
        step4:- Go to /administrator-panel
        Step5:- Delete user name Carlos

Result:- Access to admin pannel and we can add or delete user from the database

Root Cause:-The admin functionality was exposed because:

        1) Sensitive endpoints were disclosed inside robots.txt, which is publicly accessible.

        2) The admin panel had no authentication or authorization controls, allowing anyone who discovered the URL to access privileged functions.

Fix:- Protect admin functionality with proper authentication and authorization, and avoid disclosing sensitive paths in publicly accessible files such as robots.txt.
